## Item 1: the seam

- Cause: plausible. The maker probe (maker-p5-fix-cutout.log lines 20-33) shows raw row 1364 empty in one 3072 x 3072 read and full in a strip read. SwiftShader shows no empty row.
  I did not re-run the probe. What I checked agrees with it: the 4 RED assets show the same row 569 with 596, 58, 440, and 30 solid columns, and the delivered files show the same column counts now with alpha 255.0.
- The loss is size specific. My detector finds 0 seam rows in 52 older PNGs cut at 1024 x 1200 (week1/cast, week1/gestures, week2-7/gestures). A fault in the row arithmetic would hit every size.
- Fix: correct and local. `readStrips` (src/render/cutout.ts) reads strips of at most 64 rows and joins them in the layout of one whole read. src/render/page.ts replaces one call. `resolveStraight` is unchanged.
- Proof: my detector (every row; at least 8 columns whose neighbours above and below are alpha 255; mean alpha below 229.5) finds 0 seam rows in all 29 props PNGs. It is not vacuous:
  a copy of each real alpha with row 569 set to 170 is flagged for the sun, flower, easel, and kite. The real checker prints the same words as the maker RED log for the injected sun.
  A seam of alpha 240 passes by design. The 8x picture on magenta shows no line at row 569 of the sun or the flower.
- Re-cut at HEAD into /tmp: sun front, sun three-quarter, splash front, splash three-quarter, and lily pad high are md5-equal to the delivered files (5 of 5). The build is deterministic.
- Test meaning: the second new test simulates the fault and asserts it in a control line, so it fails if the function reads the buffer whole. The first test pins the strip order.
  The Red was a missing export ('readStrips is not a function'). No unit test sees the wiring in page.ts or the 64 row default (N2). The seam rule in cutout-check is the live guard, and it works only on a GPU that shows the fault.

## Item 2: the manifest elevation field (b3460c68)

- The field is additive. The CLI writes it and throws when a folder already has another elevation. The checker reads it (a missing key is 0).
- The level rule is the same expression as before. The look-down rule asks that the model reaches the foot row and does not touch the bottom edge. The old rule fails every valid look-down cutout (the near rim falls 116 px below the foot row), so a new rule was needed.
- Synthetic folders on the real script (elevation 35, foot row 874): delivered pad ok; 130 px higher FAIL ('above the foot row'); 40 px lower FAIL ('cut off at the bottom edge'); 20 px lower ok (the rule cannot see a small shift).
  The same PNG in a level folder (foot row 1008) FAIL ('lowest opaque row 990, foot row 1008'). So no level check is weakened (N3).
- The CLI fit check ignores the bottom edge, so the brief command (margin 16) wrote a clipped PNG with no error (N4). The nested manifest skip needs four calls and has no wrapper (N5).

